                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hey Team Jolly Roger, even though this game has a dormant community, I appreciate that you updated the game as of August 13, which is only a few months before I wrote this (Oct. 13, 2026 @ 00:00 CDT). \n\nNow onto what I like about the game:\n1. The hard sci-fi aesthetics. The game features orbital mechanics and optional elliptical orbits that while are unrealistic are a very good puzzle to solve when targeting your weapons.\n2. The game natively supports Linux! Team Jolly Rodger could've been like every other game dev company and force you to use Proton, but this game runs right out the box with no modifications!\n3. The game is still updated to this day, as I previously mentioned.\n\nHowever, there are a few suggestions I have:\n1. Please add planet colonization because there are barren planets and I think it would add even more action to the game. I would recommend a toggleable setting that adds this in case players want to play a short, one-planet game.\n2. Keep updating this game! Compared to the alternative Worbital, I really like this game's hard sci-fi and realistic-but-stylized graphics.",
